{{also|unilatéral}}
==English==

===Etymology===
A modern creation (circa 1802), from {{der|en|NL.|ūnilaterālis|t=one-sided}}, from {{der|en|la|ūnus|t=one}} + {{m|la|laterālis|t=sided, lateral}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌjuːnɪˈlætərəl/}}
** {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|[ˌjʉː.nɪˈlæt.ə.ɹɫ̩]|[ˌjʉː.nɪˈlæt͡ʃ.ɹɫ̩]}}
** {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|[ˌjʉː.nəˈɫæɾ.ɚ.ɻɫ̩]}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-unilateral.wav|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ætəɹəl|s=5}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Done by one [[side]] only.
# Affecting only one side of the body.
# Binding or affecting one party only.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|one-sided}}

